From: SiliconLoop closed-loop development
Subject: [PATCH 0018] ai-agent: skill v2 - make the recover_task step explicit

Incremental on 0017 (skill_loader.c already touched there). The M2/M3
skill told the model to "propose recover_task when the judgement is
stall" but the step list ended at "5. write_file the report" - and a
report write is a terminal local-tool shortcut in agent_loop, so the
model never got a round where it could call the tool. The 11-04
overnight B rounds confirmed it: 3/3 completed diagnoses judged stall
correctly, 0/3 called recover_task (0 recoveries).

Fix: step 5 becomes the conditional recover_task call (resume on
buggy_app, only on a stall verdict) and the report write moves to step
6, so the action happens BEFORE the terminal write. The inline skills
summary (B3) gets the same step and now names all six report sections -
it was listing only four, so heartbeat reports were four-section.

Skills summary grows ~230 B to ~1.47 KB (skills_buf is 1536 B); the
existing clamp keeps a truncation from writing out of bounds.

Verified on board 2026-11-04: B round shows recover_task executed and
{"result":"recovered"} (see docs/evidence/2026-11-04/).
--- a/src/tools/skill_loader.c
+++ b/src/tools/skill_loader.c
@@ -123,7 +123,11 @@
     "2. run_shell \"ps\" - every task and its state\n" \
     "3. run_shell \"free\" - heap total, used, free\n" \
     "4. read_file " AGENT_DATA_DIR "/evidence/heartbeat.txt again\n" \
-    "5. write_file the report to " AGENT_DATA_DIR "/evidence/report.md\n\n" \
+    "5. If the judgement below is stall: call recover_task once with " \
+    "action \"resume\" and target \"buggy_app\", and record its one-line " \
+    "JSON result. Skip this step on healthy or when the file is " \
+    "missing.\n" \
+    "6. write_file the report to " AGENT_DATA_DIR "/evidence/report.md\n\n" \
     "## How to judge\n" \
     "The heartbeat counter is the primary signal.\n" \
     "- Value increased between step 1 and step 4: the monitored task " \
@@ -443,10 +447,15 @@
                 "  1) read_file %s/evidence/heartbeat.txt; "
                 "2) run_shell \"ps\"; 3) run_shell \"free\"; "
                 "4) read_file heartbeat.txt again; "
